business.—Subject to the provisions of this Act, in computing a person’s income
from business in any income year, the following expenses for each separate and
distinct business shall be included under general deductions, namely:—
(a) expenditure on purchase of raw materials, stock in trade, purchase of
goods for the purpose of business and for use in business, and any stock in trade
written off;
